{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Reverse"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_const_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_const_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LaurentBoundedness.lean#L155-L159","doc":"The constant is `P.coeff m`, spelled without `reflect`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_const_of_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_const_of_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LaurentBoundedness.lean#L131-L153","doc":"**A Laurent polynomial bounded on `(0, ∞)` is constant there.**\n\nThe constant is named: it is `(reflect m P).coeff 0`, which is `P.coeff m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.laurent_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LaurentBoundedness.lean#L119-L129","doc":"**The reflection identity.**  `P(x)/x^m` IS an honest polynomial, read at\n`1/x`.  This is what removes the need for a second asymptotic argument at the\n`x → 0⁺` end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.eq_const_of_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.eq_const_of_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LaurentBoundedness.lean#L105-L117","doc":"A real polynomial bounded near `+∞` is constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.degree_le_of_bounded_div_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LaurentBoundedness.degree_le_of_bounded_div_pow","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LaurentBoundedness.lean#L92-L103","doc":"If `P(x)/x^m` is bounded near `+∞` then `deg P ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}